      "text_raw": "The sigma-delta converter\nitself is a fourth-order\nMASH 2–2 converter. In\nthe first second-order loop,\nthe loop filter only pro-\ncesses the quantization\nerror. The signal amplitudes\nare therefore much smaller\nand much lower distortion\nlevels are obtained. As a\nresult, the second stage does\nnot contain the signal any\nmore. No additional sub-\ntraction is now required in\nthe coupling between both\nstages.\nIt is clear from the coefficients used, that the feedforward causes quantization noise only in\nthe feedback loop.",
      "text": "The sigma-delta converter itself is a fourth-order MASH 2–2 converter. In the first second-order loop, the loop filter only processes the quantization error. The signal amplitudes are therefore much smaller and much lower distortion levels are obtained. As a result, the second stage does not contain the signal any more. No additional subtraction is now required in the coupling between both stages. It is clear from the coefficients used, that the feedforward causes quantization noise only in the feedback loop."
    }
  ],
